<title>NETHERLANDS: New Holland '96 prov op profit margin up.</title>
<headline>New Holland '96 prov op profit margin up.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agricultural and construction equipment maker New Holland said its provisional consolidated operating profit margin was 8.9 percent in the full 1996 year compared with 8.2 percent in 1995, a statement said.</p>
<p>Full year consolidated revenues totalled $5.5 billion, up 11 percent on 1995, it said.</p>
<p>Fourth quarter 1996 consolidated revenues were $1.4 billion, up 36 percent over the fourth quarter of 1995.</p>
<p>New Holland is controlled by Italian industrial group Fiat.</p>
